    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76579" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παίδ-ευμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is reared up</i> or <i>educated</i>, i.e. 
			<i>nursling, scholar, pupil</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				887
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμεῖς] παιδεύματα θεῶν ὄντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					24d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆλα, φυλλάδος Παρνασίας παιδεύματ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1100
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντου παιδεύματα</span>, of
			fish, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				27.5
			</span></i> (lyr.): in pl., of a single object, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>thing taught, subject of instruction</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1120.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				747c
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				7.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				60.16
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1338a11
			</span></i>(pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>means of instruction</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακόν τι π. ἦν ἄρ᾽ . . ὁ πλοῦτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					54
				</span></i>
			.</div>
